.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MD5 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_md5 ,
.Nm EVP_md5_sha1
.Nd MD5 For EVP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft const EVP_MD *
.Fo EVP_md5
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft const EVP_MD *
.Fo EVP_md5_sha1
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
MD5 is a cryptographic hash function standardized in RFC 1321 and
designed by Ronald Rivest.
.Pp
The CMU Software Engineering Institute considers MD5 unsuitable for
further use since its security has been severely compromised.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_md5()
The MD5 algorithm which produces a 128-bit output from a given input.
.It EVP_md5_sha1()
A hash algorithm of SSL v3 that combines MD5 with SHA-1 as described in
RFC 6101.
.Pp
WARNING: this algorithm is not intended for non-SSL usage.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling these functions multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_MD-MD5 7
or
.Xr EVP_MD-MD5-SHA1 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return a
.Sy EVP_MD
structure that contains the implementation of the message digest.
See
.Xr EVP_MD_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_MD
structure.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
IETF RFC 1321.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr evp 7 ,
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
